      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's a combination of both, but largely dictated by established genre expectations. The *vibe*—hoodie, street smarts, carry weight—is shorthand Hollywood uses to instantly signal a world of illicit activity. If you swapped the names but kept that core energy, yes, they would still likely feel like crime drama figures because the audience associates those identifiers with that genre. To stand out, you'll need to subvert those expectations in their actions instead of just their presentation.",
